  (text "RAIL QUALIFICATION: U505/U506 are powered by DIGITAL P3V3 and sense 5 V / analog 3.3 V independently.\nP3V3_OK drives MR. CT intentionally open: 12-28 ms release delay; fault assertion has separate sensor latency.\nRAILS_OK = P3V3_OK AND PG12_N AND P5V_OK AND P3V3_A_OK. PG12_N is HIGH when the 12 V supply reports good.\nR510/R511 use 0.1% initial tolerance for 5 V recovery margin. Ripple, drift and transient budgets remain to qualify.\nThese are undervoltage monitors, not overvoltage protection. Hardware stop/watchdog/fault qualification remains unfinished."
    (at 70 490 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "b4aa4119-b763-4ef7-8013-dad9ee130a48")
  )
  (text "AUXILIARY SUPPLY DRAFT — separate from the driver VM converter.\nLM5164: 12.108 V nominal before ripple offset; Type-3 injection returns to output.\nLMR51430XF: 500 kHz FPWM, 6.8 uH / 2x22 uF starting point; no extra polymer capacitor.\nBudget: control connector 5 V / 0.5 A; fan 12 V / 0.15 A. Not a tested load rating.\nPG12_N and P3V3_OK join the independent 5 V/analog supervisors in RAILS_OK below.\nThermal-via arrays, capacitor bias derating, loop/startup tests and source protection remain open."
    (at 335 355 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "0e63645b-ed7a-4047-9205-145781f17a26")
  )
